        "original_id": "1e00dd4c-979a-50ad-9e7a-2df574ef8820",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Florida State Road 922, Bal Harbour Shops, Haulover Park, Baker's Haulover Inlet\n- Places: northeastern Miami-Dade County, Bal Harbour, Atlantic Ocean, Biscayne Bay, Collins Avenue\n- Organizations: Whitman family\n- Topics: commercial corridors, family-owned malls, parks, nude beaches, marinas\n\nFacts:\n- Florida State Road 922 is an important commercial artery in northeastern Miami-Dade County, with stores lining much of the route.\n- Bal Harbour Shops is located near the eastern terminus of Florida State Road 922.\n- Haulover Park is located on a shoal between the Atlantic Ocean and Biscayne Bay, just north of the Broad Causeway, which is Florida State Road 922, and Collins Avenue.\n- Baker's Haulover Inlet is the location of the 99-acre Haulover Park.\n- Haulover Park includes an official nude beach, recreation areas, and a marina.\n- Bal Harbour Shops is owned by the Whitman family and is one of the few remaining family-owned malls in the United States.",
